{{for|the notable passive skill|Wish for Death}} 
{{Skill infobox|id=DeathWish}}
'''Death Wish''' is a [[active skill|skill]] granted by {{il|Maw of Mischief}}, a unique {{il|Bone Helmet}}, that applies a spreading buff to your minions while channelled that improves their abilities and makes them eventually explode.

==Skill functions and interactions==
* Minions are chosen at random. Line of sight to chosen minions is not required.
* Once 13 minions are affected, the spell will continue channelling but no more minions will be added.
* Ending the channel, or casting any non-instant [[spell]] will cause all affected minions to explode, killing them instantly and triggering any "on minion death" effects, such as the {{c|mod|Minions recover 5% of Life on Minion Death}} minion defense [[Passive Mastery|passive mastery]].
* Minions that are exploded by this skill will not trigger [[Minion Instability]]'s explosion, as they never ''reach'' low life.
* The skill cannot affect "immortal" minions, minions without a life pool, or minions already prepared to explode by the skill.<ref name="Q&AMay2021"/> <br />"Immortal" minions include:
** {{sl|Spectral Spirits}} ({{il|Essence of Insanity}}).
** Agony Crawlers ({{il|Herald of Agony}}).
** Skitterbots ({{il|Summon Skitterbots}})

* Cannot target minions summoned by minions.
* The Fire damage hit scales with spell damage and can be reflected; the [[explosion]] based off of minion life does not scale with spell damage and cannot be reflected.

